From 464f45a92c6fc3fb98b59064538ba364352ba4d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: julian_lenovo_new <julian@jc84.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:48:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] config: add touchpad three-finger-drag option

Expose libinput's native 3-finger drag (`@since 1.27`) as an
`input { touchpad { three-finger-drag [fingers=3|4] } }` knob. Holding
N fingers emulates a held left button so moving them drags without a
physical press or tap-and-drag.

The symbol is resolved via dlsym at runtime rather than enabling the
`input` crate's `libinput_1_28` feature, because Ubuntu 24.04 (CI) ships
libinput 1.25. Older libinput logs a warning and ignores the setting.

Pairs with the configurable TouchpadSwipe finger counts: users can move
the default 3-finger workspace/column swipes to fingers=4 and free three
fingers for dragging (niri-wm/niri#2786).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
